h this  pore then depending on the base  composition that is currently blocking  the pore  in other words the sequence this flow of  ions is more or less blocked  leading in leading to measurable drops  in current these current drops  occur in sequence specific patterns as  some bases lead to stronger or weaker  longer or shorter changes in current  the advantages of this method include  low cost speed  long read length and a couple of other  interesting aspects such as the  potential to  directly sequence rna or to detect  chemical dna modifications  such as dna methylation a potential  issue however is that biological poor  and dna translocating enzymes  are likely to be not 100 identical  across all pores  and flow cells biological variability is  unavoidable and  potentially affects base calling quality  we are therefore currently conducting a  validation study  using the ont platform relying  on the same seven ground truth reference  strains we have used previously  in our published validation studies  this slide outlines the study design the  seven  samples were extracted with suitable dna  extraction methods from three different  vendors resulting in a total of 21 dna  extracts  each extract is aliquoted and sent to  three partner labs  for ngs library preparation and  sequencing at an insert size of 10 kb  using ont rapid barcoding kits and the r  10.3 flow cells  raw data are then uploaded to the iris  cloud and subjected to the standard  analysis workflow  which consists of qc de novo assembly  microbial identification  core genome embolicity amr marker  prediction predictive ast and plasma  typing  preliminary data and these are truly hot  of the press suggest a fair amount of  variability in terms of output  and read quality between partner labs  nevertheless basic nucleotide identity  between the resulting genome assemblies  and the ground truth remain high and  this is an important prerequisite for  downstream analyses  it's also important to note that